Package: predictlearn
Title: Machine Learning Discovery of Structure in PLS-SEM Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Simon", "Dang", email = "simon.hdang@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Takes raw indicator data, estimates a PLS-SEM measurement model,
    extracts latent variable scores, and then searches for structural
    relationships the researcher did not hypothesize. Bayesian network
    structure learning identifies candidate arcs under theory-derived
    constraints; MARS and generalized additive models probe the surviving
    relationships for non-linearity; candidate models are compared against the
    theoretical baseline on information criteria and out-of-sample error.
    Implements the procedure of Richter and Tudoran (2024) with a browser-based
    interface that runs locally.
